  "snapshot": "data_science",
  "instruction": "Using Jupyter Notebook, create a new notebook named `missing_value_imputation.ipynb` under `/home/user/analysis_results/`. The dataset `data.csv` is already in that folder. In the notebook, load the dataset using pandas. Identify all columns with missing values (for example, `MonthlyIncome`, `NumberOfDependents`). Impute missing `MonthlyIncome` values with the median computed within each age group: '<40', '40–60', '>60'. Fill missing `NumberOfDependents` values with its mode. Save the cleaned dataset as `imputed_data.csv` in the same directory and also write a summary text file named `imputation_summary.txt` that lists which columns had missing values before imputation.",
  "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/plotly/datasets/refs/heads/master/data.csv",

  "config": [
